                <pb facs="0757" n="647" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg647"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Ryan to Mr.
                            Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-07-29"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 29, 1890</date>.
                        (Received July 30.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Ryan reports that he has seen a telegram just received from Ezeta to his
                    special agent in Mexico in relation to the suppression of telegrams, and which
                    reads: “I have ordered telegrams of Mexican and American Governments to be
                    passed, but lines in Guatemala are broken. A ship might be gotten by the
                    American minister to transport his communications to San José.”</p>
            </div>
